  "details": "Please see the attached screenshots to explain the issue.\n\nI have an avatar which is reported as 4 materials in the local SDK test build and in the SDK, but as 5 material slots when uploaded. This occurs when a skinned mesh renderer has more material slots than sub-meshes.\n\n# Avatar setup explained\n\n- `Armature`\n\n- `Body` (skinned mesh renderer): 2 materials (`Salt_Face`, `Salt_Face_Effect`)\n\n- `Hair`(skinned mesh renderer): 2 materials (`Salt_Hair`, `Salt_Hair_FakeShadow`); **1 sub-mesh**\n\n- `Hair_Base` (skinned mesh renderer): 1 materials (`Salt_Hair`)\n\n# Steps to reproduce\n\nThis is how I did this:\n\n1. I got the Salt_v1.01 avatar by komado from BOOTH (https://komado.booth.pm/items/8962830).\n\n2. I created a new VRChat SDK 3.10.6 project with d4rkAvatarOptimizer v4.7.2 and other avatar dependencies added from ALCOM.\n\n3. I added the Salt prefab to the scene. I deleted anything but `Armature`, `Base`, `Hair`, `Hair_Base` gameobjects. `Hair` will have two materials (`Salt_Hair`, `Salt_Hair_FakeShadow`; 1 submesh), `Hair_Base` has one material shared (`Salt_Hair`) shared with `Hair` gameobject.\n\n4. (Optional, not required) I added d4rkAvatarOptimizer component to the avatar (as a gameobject or on the avatar root), basic/standard optimizations with \"Delete Unused GameObjects\" checked.\n\n5. Build & Test.\n\n6. Build & Publish (upload).\n\n7. Compare the avatar performance details of the uploaded avatar and the SDK test avatar in the VRChat client (Build `1939`).\n\n# Expected result\n\nSDK & local SDK test avatar should report 5 material slots in the VRChat client. The uploaded avatar should report 5 material slots too.\n\n# Actual result\n\nSDK & local SDK test avatar both report 4 material slots; **missing one material slot**. The uploaded avatar reports 5 material slots.\n\n# Additional information\n\nd4rkAvatarOptimizer is not required to reproduce this bug. It should be reproducible with VRChat SDK 3.10.6 and the current live branch VRChat 2026.4.1 (Build `1939`) client alone.\n\nI have confirmed the issue is not with the material shaders used.\n\nThe default Salt avatar base FBX does not setup a 2nd material slot on the `Hair` renderer by default, this extra material slot was added to the prefab by the creator of the base for a lilToon fake shadow.\n\nRelated d4rkAvatarOptimizer v4.6.0 change: https://github.com/d4rkc0d3r/d4rkAvatarOptimizer/pull/194\n\nRelated d4rkAvatarOptimizer changelog: https://github.com/d4rkc0d3r/d4rkAvatarOptimizer/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#v460\n\nI can provide private avatar IDs for minimal repro avatar versions on request, if specified which version(s).\n\nVRChat SDK - Avatars 3.10.6. d4rkAvatarOptimizer versions `4.5.4`, `4.6.0` and `4.7.2` (latest). The latter two d4rkAvatarOptimizer versions share the same behavior. VRChat 2026.4.1 Build `1939` on Windows.",
